# <type>: <subject> (max 50 chars)
# |<----  Using a Maximum Of 50 Characters  ---->|

# Body: Explain *what* and *why* (not *how*), wrap at 72 chars
# |<----   Try To Limit Each Line to a Maximum Of 72 Characters   ---->|

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#   feat     New feature
#   fix      Bug fix
#   docs     Documentation only
#   style    Formatting, no code change
#   refactor Code change, no new feature or bug fix
#   perf     Performance improvement
#   test     Adding/updating tests
#   chore    Maintenance, dependencies, configs
#   ci       CI/CD changes
#   build    Build system changes
#
# Remember:
#   - Capitalize the subject line
#   - Do not end the subject line with a period
#   - Use imperative mood: "Add feature" not "Added feature"
#   - Separate subject from body with a blank line
#   - Body should explain what and why, not how
#   - Reference issues at the bottom: "Fixes #123"
#
# Example:
#   feat: Add user authentication
#
#   Implement JWT-based authentication to secure API endpoints.
#   Users can now register and login with email/password.
#
#   - Add /auth/register and /auth/login endpoints
#   - Store hashed passwords with bcrypt
#   - Return JWT token on successful login
#
#   Fixes #42
